{"id":"c2b61b7b-102a-482f-a6a7-8cbdb6cac28d","title":"Generated quiz 2025-08-28 12:04:28","fetched":"2026-10-23T23:58:46.660Z","questions":[{"id":"0aa018e9-c064-4950-9037-278bbfb2c9cf","title":"Provide Python implementations (Question 25, ITE 2024 Y11)","isPublished":true,"publishDate":"2025-04-29T03:07:46.392Z","syllabusId":"79cc4e36-7dc8-43d3-abdc-d4320853a7c8","stimulusContentItemCollection":{"id":"bd59939d-b86f-457f-80fe-cdea9caf9df8","items":[{"id":"9e86e5bd-d297-48af-8c99-20efc03ad763","updatedDate":"2025-04-30T23:49:01.821Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Consider the following class diagram which models an employee management system:</span></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://assets.gradeo.com.au/asset/edb989f6-09ea-4aa6-bd41-d011f99cc86e\"></p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>You can assume:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>The display_info() method prints the properties of the object created from that class.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>The Manager has a property called subordinates which stores an array of Employee objects representing the employees who report to that manager.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>The add_subordinate() method adds a given Employee object to the subordinates property of that Manager object.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>You do not need to enforce the relationship cardinalities (1..1, 1..*) between Employee and Manager objects.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["9e86e5bd-d297-48af-8c99-20efc03ad763"]},"publisher":{"id":"185bbf24-2f3a-45e7-af59-eb9b643e6ac0","name":"Independent Trials","isPremium":true,"isAIGenerated":false,"isChangeable":true,"jurisdiction":{"id":"58c4dd02-8091-4797-aeae-d4c81cea5058","name":"NSW"},"logoFile":{"id":"6cde5036-0b95-43d0-9e41-96b10837d695","url":"https://assets.gradeo.com.au/asset/aa367e7e-d075-4808-9128-23998e4dcff8"}},"dynamicFields":null,"copyrightText":null,"visibility":"PUBLIC","school":null,"systemId":null,"system":null,"isPublisherLocked":false,"parts":[{"id":"b30c0c25-bb96-4e77-98a2-b6fb376c9399","displayIndex":0,"title":"Question 25","metadata":{"id":"84114f3e-f4dd-43dc-9d22-9d6b0b600a36","mark":5,"syllabus":{"id":"79cc4e36-7dc8-43d3-abdc-d4320853a7c8","title":"Software Engineering","description":"Software Engineering Stage 6 Syllabus 2022","gradeFrom":11,"gradeTo":11,"coverageLabel":null,"curriculumCode":null,"curriculumVersion":null,"gradingScaleName":null,"publishedYear":null,"publishedDate":null},"band":null,"outcomeIds":["bc9a626c-b01b-4ff3-a207-dd283dfd960e"],"topicIds":["efd3637b-a6a9-4eb9-b911-1dc5eaaf1862"],"subtopicIds":["ed11bcf8-bd7c-4316-b585-4caebf6f461e"],"subtopicItemIds":["a1109fa5-02f0-4781-9e5a-c45083788eb6"],"bandIds":["aaa06251-1928-4762-aba4-64e6294915d1","aaf1a4a3-9deb-47d7-8d93-f6d7254c5da1","ce3fff6b-6d49-4ff5-b2d7-5a31c14d9544"]},"content":{"id":"7ab70ed7-629f-412e-a82b-9d3bef24a627","contentItemCollection":{"id":"5f2d5984-07dc-46b5-9018-50800fd78dfc","items":[{"id":"595d3acc-ba86-4238-90dd-b2d71b50bde2","updatedDate":"2025-04-30T23:48:52.719Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Provide Python implementations for each of the Employee, Manager and Developer classes.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["595d3acc-ba86-4238-90dd-b2d71b50bde2"]},"contentItemMetadata":null},"answer":{"id":"1470629e-3166-4de1-bd6f-61bf20c35864","parameters":{"version":0,"type":"CODING","settings":{"showExecutionOutput":false,"highlightSyntax":false},"language":"PYTHON","defaultCode":null},"files":null},"markingCriteriaContentItem":{"id":"c69b11f3-8036-41bc-9061-6fe051a71ef8","updatedDate":"2025-04-29T01:13:29.027Z","files":null,"type":"MARKING_CRITERIA","criteria":[{"criterion":"<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Provides correct definitions for ALL of the three classes in Python, providing at least the following for each class:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>Employee</span></p>\n</li>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>__init__ method to initialise and populate the object's properties</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>display_info method to print the object's properties</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>Manager</span></p>\n</li>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>__init__ method calls super then initialises and populates the object's properties</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>add_subordinate method to append an Employee object to the subordinate array</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>Developer</span></p>\n</li>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>__init__ method calls super then initialises and populates the object's properties</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>display_info method calls super and also prints the specialisation value</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","point":"5"},{"criterion":"<p>Provides substantially correct definitions for ALL of the three classes in Python, which may contain some minor errors or omissions.</p>","point":"4"},{"criterion":"<p>Provides substantially correct definitions for AT LEAST TWO of the three classes in Python, which may contain some minor errors or omissions.</p>","point":"3"},{"criterion":"<p><strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-5e140540-7fff-4ac5-e736-982eb2c2990c\"><span>An attempt at providing definitions for AT LEAST TWO of the three classes in Python.</span></strong></p>","point":"2"},{"criterion":"<p>An attempt at providing a definition for AT LEAST ONE of the three classes in Python.</p>","point":"1"}]},"markingRubricContentItem":{"id":"1276553f-d01f-4985-b422-e41d0aba3574","updatedDate":"2025-04-30T23:48:52.798Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.gradeo.com.au/asset/bd05b1bb-59f1-45de-8129-448550d4ce0e\"></p>"},"markingGuidanceContentItem":null,"sampleAnswerContentItem":null}]},{"id":"d5011f0a-2144-40e0-a363-1949a8654c35","title":"Pseudocode Algorithm (Question 20, ITE 2024 Y11)","isPublished":true,"publishDate":"2025-04-29T03:18:50.055Z","syllabusId":"79cc4e36-7dc8-43d3-abdc-d4320853a7c8","stimulusContentItemCollection":{"id":"265491fd-dfee-49ef-ac8e-3f8d975f9aa5","items":[{"id":"398c1913-7eec-413e-a2fe-1f39d1aa51f0","updatedDate":"2025-04-30T23:46:33.032Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>A &lsquo;magic square&rsquo; is a grid with a width and height of </span><span>n</span><span>, containing the numbers from 1 to </span><span>n</span><span>2</span><span>. Each row, column, and diagonal adds up to the same sum. For example, in the grid below </span><span>n</span><span> is 3; the grid contains the numbers 1-9, and every row, column, and diagonal adds up to 15.</span></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://assets.gradeo.com.au/asset/0b61efb6-d02d-49bb-bd76-ca64a38b107c\"></p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["398c1913-7eec-413e-a2fe-1f39d1aa51f0"]},"publisher":{"id":"185bbf24-2f3a-45e7-af59-eb9b643e6ac0","name":"Independent Trials","isPremium":true,"isAIGenerated":false,"isChangeable":true,"jurisdiction":{"id":"58c4dd02-8091-4797-aeae-d4c81cea5058","name":"NSW"},"logoFile":{"id":"6cde5036-0b95-43d0-9e41-96b10837d695","url":"https://assets.gradeo.com.au/asset/aa367e7e-d075-4808-9128-23998e4dcff8"}},"dynamicFields":null,"copyrightText":null,"visibility":"PUBLIC","school":null,"systemId":null,"system":null,"isPublisherLocked":false,"parts":[{"id":"b8967ee9-b473-495f-b45e-ea51c3f9a100","displayIndex":0,"title":"Question 20","metadata":{"id":"5959821c-7c6c-4924-abe8-1980703f2103","mark":5,"syllabus":{"id":"79cc4e36-7dc8-43d3-abdc-d4320853a7c8","title":"Software Engineering","description":"Software Engineering Stage 6 Syllabus 2022","gradeFrom":11,"gradeTo":11,"coverageLabel":null,"curriculumCode":null,"curriculumVersion":null,"gradingScaleName":null,"publishedYear":null,"publishedDate":null},"band":null,"outcomeIds":["bc9a626c-b01b-4ff3-a207-dd283dfd960e"],"topicIds":["f98ac64a-475c-4740-aa86-d46160bd18bf"],"subtopicIds":["086a4aa7-5b89-4db8-8792-512c273e4fd1"],"subtopicItemIds":["b431d396-ba1d-486a-8a7b-8bca3f354eac"],"bandIds":["aaa06251-1928-4762-aba4-64e6294915d1","aaf1a4a3-9deb-47d7-8d93-f6d7254c5da1","ce3fff6b-6d49-4ff5-b2d7-5a31c14d9544"]},"content":{"id":"5fc65047-74c4-4b1f-86ba-f74239e597f6","contentItemCollection":{"id":"79ea7a19-3130-48a9-8f03-07bb229e17f7","items":[{"id":"4924b4c4-6929-4e91-afe8-e5939a4abbd2","updatedDate":"2025-04-30T23:46:28.848Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p>Write an algorithm in pseudocode for a function which, when passed a 2D array of integers called &ldquo;square&rdquo;, will return True if the square is &ldquo;magic&rdquo; and False otherwise.</p>"}],"itemIdOrder":["4924b4c4-6929-4e91-afe8-e5939a4abbd2"]},"contentItemMetadata":null},"answer":{"id":"0a37ec8b-d879-4a25-ae70-2fbe7e529e22","parameters":{"version":0,"type":"CODING","settings":{"showExecutionOutput":false,"highlightSyntax":false},"language":"PYTHON","defaultCode":null},"files":null},"markingCriteriaContentItem":{"id":"ffbf09d3-18c9-4692-acf9-a77456c121ab","updatedDate":"2025-04-29T01:02:49.354Z","files":null,"type":"MARKING_CRITERIA","criteria":[{"criterion":"<p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Creates a substantially correct algorithm, using NESA&rsquo;s format for pseudocode, which attempts all of the following:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>Checks the size of the 2D array</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>Iterates through the 2D array</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>Calculates the sum for each row and column</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>Calculates the sum for each diagonal</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>Returns true if all sums are equal</span></p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span>Returns false otherwise</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>","point":"5"},{"criterion":"<p>Creates an algorithm in pseudocode which attempts at least four of the above criteria.</p>","point":"4"},{"criterion":"<p>Creates an algorithm, or language-specific code, which attempts at least three of the above criteria.</p>","point":"3"},{"criterion":"<p>Creates an algorithm or code which includes some of the required logic for two or more of the above criteria.</p>","point":"2"},{"criterion":"<p>Creates an algorithm or code which addresses some part of the question.</p>","point":"1"}]},"markingRubricContentItem":{"id":"3fb29283-7567-4fb3-9dc7-cac7c1aa2855","updatedDate":"2025-04-30T23:46:46.541Z","files":null,"type":"RICH_TEXT","text":"<p><img src=\"https://assets.gradeo.com.au/asset/c9b59de4-d43e-4394-bcba-c8a2200cc2fe\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://assets.gradeo.com.au/asset/1c9e4b65-c996-4666-9c93-c835ebe4ce99\"></p>"},"markingGuidanceContentItem":null,"sampleAnswerContentItem":null}]}],"answers_error":"page.evaluate: Error: 403 marking-session/question-part-aggregated-by-student/c2b61b7b-102a-482f-a6a7-8cbdb6cac28d","state_error":"page.evaluate: Error: 403 marking-session/state-participant/c2b61b7b-102a-482f-a6a7-8cbdb6cac28d"}